      "description": "Career Prospects and Further Study This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience on our website. Learn more Got it! Students Prospective Students Current Students Honour List Staff Staff Portal Student Information eServices Short Courses eServices Moodle Webmail Venue Booking Alumni Alumni Community Graduates Partners Job Posting for Alumni Job Posting for Students Graduate Verification Professional course certificate inquiry Platform Suppliers Database Public Tender Consulta Escrita Media News Portal Press Release Events Visitors New Professional/ Vocational/ Short Courses Job Vacancies Venues for Meeting & Event Location of UTM Explore UTM UTM Campus Virtual Tour Contact Us Contact Us Suggestions and Comments Enquiry Form English English 繁體 简体 Português About UTM General Information Mission Statement UTM Council Rector Message Recognitions Organisational Law & General Rules of UTM Staff Annual Report UTM Videos Our Campus First Phase of Macao-Hengqin International Education (University) Town Teaching Site Explore UTM Open Day Quality Assurance Policy Public Services and Organizational Performance Appraisal System Souvenirs Teaching & Learning Programmes Macao Higher Education Policies and Regulations Faculty of Innovative Hospitality Management Faculty of Creative Tourism and Intelligent Technologies Institute of Executive and Professional Development Centre for Education Quality Management Global Centre for Tourism Education and Training UTM-CRCS Centre for Innovative Talent Development Facilities Training Units We Care Ideation Lab iRetail Lab Admission Postgraduate Programmes Undergraduate Programmes Scholarships & Fellowships Global Exposure Information Guide for Non-local Students Research International Centre for Tourism and Hospitality Research Academic Publication Tourism Education Student Summit Global Network Introduction Membership Global Partners Global Exposure Greater Bay Area Hengqin Guangdong-Macao in-depth cooperation zone Overview of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area Tourism Education and Training Base for the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area The Alliance for Developing Macao into the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area Tourism Education and Training Base Tourism Professional Education Alliance of Greater Bay Area Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao University Tourism Research Alliance Extension of Macao Base One Examination Multiple Certificates Press Release Career Prospects and Further Study Home Career Prospects and Further Study Ready for employment UTM degree graduates are in demand among employers, not only for their knowledge and competence in the field of tourism and hospitality, but also for their versatility in other industry sectors as well as their ‘soft skills’ gained from the University. UTM’s degree curriculums are structured with a balance of both theoretical and practical components, thus giving our graduates a competitive edge upon their graduation. The University’s latest UTM Alumni Employment Survey in 2021 covering alumni graduated in 2018 or before indicated that some 23% alumni were employed as “senior level or higher” roles. More than 3,600 alumni responded and the overall response rate stood at 47%. About 58% employed respondents were working in the tourism and hospitality industry, with majority engaged in mega integrated resorts and entertainment complexes. Some 13% alumni respondents reported they were working in public administration. The median salary of alumni respondents was significantly higher than MOP15,800 median monthly earnings of the overall Macao workforce in 2021 (source: Statistics and Census Service). Respondents graduated between 1995 and 2000 had the highest median salary, at MOP57,500. The median wage level was most modest among those graduated between 2016 and 2018, standing at MOP20,500. Postgraduate opportunities to TOP universities University graduation is the starting point, not the endpoint, of higher education. Many graduates choose to pursue further studies to gain deeper professional knowledge and skills for their future careers. According to the latest UTM Alumni Employment Survey, a considerable proportion of graduates have advanced to higher degrees. Based on the QS World University Rankings 2026, 45% of graduates were admitted to the world's top 100 universities, and 29% were admitted to the world's top 50 universities—a truly encouraging achievement. Top universities that have admitted UTM graduates include, but are not limited to: National University of Singapore, The University of Hong Kong, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, Peking University, Cornell University, The University of Melbourne, The University of New South Wales, The University of Sydney, University of Toronto, The Australian National University, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, The University of Edinburgh, The University of Manchester, etc. With opportunities spanning 25 countries and regions and 177 institutions, the path to postgraduate studies at world-leading universities is broader than ever. Admission Postgraduate Programmes Undergraduate Programmes Scholarships & Fellowships Global Exposure Information Guide for Non-local Students Courses & Campus Global Centre for Tourism Education and Training International Centre for Tourism and Hospitality Research Educational Restaurant Short-term Courses Undergraduate Programmes See Also Tourism Education Student Summit Alumni Community Job Posting for Alumni Job Posting for Students Information About Faculty of Innovative Hospitality Management Faculty of Creative Tourism and Intelligent Technologies Institute of Executive and Professional Development UTM Library Pousada de Mong-Há – Educational Hotel Educational Residence Educational Restaurant UTM Café My Green Campus News New Professional/ Vocational/ Short Courses Accepted List of IEPD Courses Job Vacancies News Portal Quick Link Bad Weather Arrangements Payment Methods for Degree Programmes Public Tender Programmes Macao Higher Education Policies and Regulations UTM Scholar Hub Joint Admission Examination for Macao Four Higher Education Institutions Contact Us Mong-Há Campus : Colina de Mong-Há, Macau, China Taipa Campus: Avenida Padre Tomás Pereira,S.N.,Taipa, Macau, China (View Map) © Copyright 2017. All Rights Reserved. Sitemap Privacy Policy"
